              "role": "headliner",
              "socialMedia": [],
              "bio": "In Slavic Folklore, the rusalki are mythical water-bound beings, the trapped soul of women who died violent deaths in the water where they reside. These folktales often tell the stories of women who were tragically murdered at the hands of men. They linger around bodies of water waiting to lure men to the depths in a hypnotic revenge. Written and directed by Eva Blackwell Rogelj. Produced by Zara Trott. Funded by The MiraBan Independent Film Fund. Selected by Aesthetica Film Festival."
